ected::error","note":"Returns a reference to the stored value."},{"label":"std::unexpected::swap","note":"Swaps the stored values, as if by using std::swap; swap(error(), other.error());."},{"label":"operator==(std::unexpected)","note":"Compares the stored values, as if by return x.error() == y.error()."},{"label":"swap(std::unexpected)","note":"Equivalent to x.swap(y).","children":[{"label":"Deduction guides","note":"The deduction guide is provided for unexpected to allow deduction from the constructor argument."},{"label":"Notes","note":"Prior to C++17, the name std::unexpected denoted the function called by the C++ runtime when a dynamic exception specification was violated."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also"}]}]},"standards":["C++23"],"wordCount":725,"codeBlockCount":2}
